{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 30,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now they that are younger than I have me in derision,\nWhose fathers I disdained to set with the dogs of my flock.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yea, the strength of their hands, whereto should it profit me?\nMen in whom ripe age is perished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are gaunt with want and famine;They gnaw the dry ground, in the gloom of wasteness and desolation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They pluck salt-wort by the bushes;\nAnd the roots of the broom are their food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are driven forth from the midst ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ";\nThey cry after them as after a thief;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that they dwell in frightful valleys,\nIn holes of the earth and of the rocks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Among the bushes they bray;\nUnder the nettles they are gathered together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " children of fools, yea, children of base men;\nThey were scourged out of the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now I am become their song,\nYea, I am a byword unto them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They abhor me, they stand aloof from me,\nAnd spare not to spit in my face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he hath loosed his cord, and afflicted me;\nAnd they have cast off the bridle before me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Upon my right hand rise the rabble;\nThey thrust aside my feet,\nAnd they cast up against me their ways of destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They mar my path,\nThey set forward my calamity,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " men that have no helper.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As through a wide breach they come:\nIn the midst of the ruin they roll themselves ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "upon me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Terrors are turned upon me;They chase mine honor as the wind;\nAnd my welfare is passed away as a cloud.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now my soul is poured out within me;\nDays of affliction have taken hold upon me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the night season my bones are pierced in me,\nAnd the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "pains",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that gnaw me take no rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God’s",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " great force is my garment disfigured;\nIt bindeth me about as the collar of my coat.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath cast me into the mire,\nAnd I am become like dust and ashes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I cry unto thee, and thou dost not answer me:\nI stand up, and thou gazest at me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou art turned to be cruel to me;\nWith the might of thy hand thou persecutest me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou liftest me up to the wind, thou causest me to ride ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "upon it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ";\nAnd thou dissolvest me in the storm.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I know that thou wilt bring me to death,\nAnd to the house appointed for all living.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Howbeit doth not one stretch out the hand in his fall?\nOr in his calamity therefore cry for help?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Did not I weep for him that was in trouble?\nWas not my soul grieved for the needy?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I looked for good, then evil came;\nAnd when I waited for light, there came darkness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My heart is troubled, and resteth not;\nDays of affliction are come upon me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I go mourning without the sun:\nI stand up in the assembly, and cry for help.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am a brother to jackals,\nAnd a companion to ostriches.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My skin is black, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and falleth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from me,\nAnd my bones are burned with heat.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.30.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore is my harp ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "turned",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to mourning,\nAnd my pipe into the voice of them that weep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
